WEBVTT

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.540
What's this?

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.410
It's from Morrigan.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.790
Miss Mariah was given one, too.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.870
It's from Grandmother Morrigan?

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.040
But why did you have it, Gregory-<i>sensei</i>?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.870
W-Well, Morrigan is an old friend of mine.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.580
Big sister, what does it say?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.160
Well, um...

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.790
"If I can gather three Artifacts--

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.500
the Glyph of the Wind God,
the Ring of the Thunder God,

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.120
and the Violin of the Earth God--
I will release Hoshisato Maeve."

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.950
Mother will be released from the village?

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.080
Really?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.160
You girls have a right to
take part in this operation.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.540
What do you say?

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.870
I'm in, of course! After all, I am...

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:01.290
...she who steals sadness, and turns it
into smiles, the master thief Hatena!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:31.660
"Several days later..."

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.500
"Several days later..."
Then Maeve is not currently at the
Hoshisato mansion, just as Ms. Li said?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.200
Then Maeve is not currently at the
Hoshisato mansion, just as Ms. Li said?

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.870
Yes. The only ones there right now are children.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.410
That troublesome Hoshisato Mamoru
is booked with performances,

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.160
and frequently appears to be out of the country.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.040
Then why don't we take that treasure from them?

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.410
If you need men, I can provide them.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:56.540
The Hoshisato mansion is a
treasure mine. A little risk is nothing.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.160
Hmm... There is one thing
I'd like to confirm first.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.160
What do you want in return for this information?

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.450
We want nothing.
We are still such a small organization.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.870
Being allowed to join you in
this gathering is more than enough.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.160
What was your name, again?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.290
My name is Michelle Li.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:25.700
Michelle, huh? I'll remember that.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.830
Thank you very much.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.160
Australia?

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.950
Mm-hmm, Master Gregory and I have a show there.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.120
So what about the Artifacts
we need to get Mother back?

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.540
It's <i>for </i>an Artifact.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.950
We found out where one of
the three Artifacts we have to find,

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.000
the Violin of the Earth God, is located.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.750
So then, you're saying...

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.500
...it's in Australia?

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:58.700
Correct, my precious. So we decided
to do an overseas performance.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:02.790
Wait, Father! I'll steal the Artifact!

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:07.080
Makoto and Yumemi both said they'd help me.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.200
Do you want to tag along to our overseas show?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:15.290
Yes! I'm definitely coming! I will--
the master thief Hatena will steal it!

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.160
Then we'll get Mother back.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.790
Mm-hmm. Makoto-<i>kun</i>, what about you?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:26.500
I'm coming, of course. I am the
master thief Hatena's partner, after all.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.370
It's so cold!

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.660
What is it, winter here?

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.790
This is the southern hemisphere,
so it stands to reason, doesn't it?

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:42.120
Oh, that's right, huh?

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.540
Up to now, I've always come
to Australia during winter in Japan.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.450
Mamoru-<i>sama</i>, if we just stand around here,

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:54.950
the mistresses are going to catch colds.
Let's hurry off to our lodgings.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:05:00.540
Right. Master Gregory arrived first,
and he's supposed to pick us up.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.160
I hope I haven't kept you waiting.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:09.160
It took some time finding a
rental car that could fit everyone in it.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.000
Sir Camelot!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:28.370
Allow me to introduce you.
This is Bryan, the son of an old friend.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:33.200
When I mentioned I was coming to
Australia, he insisted that I stop by.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.830
And this is my unworthy apprentice--

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:41.830
Nice to meet you, Mr. Hoshisato. I am Bryan.
It is an honor to meet you.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:43.660
H-Hi there.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.830
Yes, come in.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.500
Gregory-<i>sensei</i>!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:58.080
Ho, no sooner do we arrive
than you're hard at work again.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.700
I am trying to master
this even a little bit more.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:05.750
If only Mamoru worked
a hundredth as hard as you do...

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:11.160
Tell you what, as a reward to
my young and diligent apprentice,

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:14.370
I will show you my very best magic trick.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.620
Do you mean it?

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.410
Mm-hmm. Watch closely now.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:25.910
Look.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:31.950
My very best magic trick
is one that uses this dove.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:36.080
Were you expecting something
other than this basic, classic trick?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.250
N-No, not at all...

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.250
This is the very first trick I learned,

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:47.540
as well as being the trick I was worst at.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.500
Huh?

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:53.290
However, as I kept practicing it over
and over, and performed it on stage,

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:57.700
at some point, I realized that
I no longer felt it was my worst trick!

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:02.250
For me, that led to a great deal of confidence.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:15.450
The trick I practiced the most is
what I believe to be my best trick.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.500
Feelings are something
you can visibly see, right?

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.790
The essence of magic is
in something that is not seen.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:26.290
It is in the repeated
practicing that no one ever sees--

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:29.750
Wait, you're better off figuring
the rest out on your own.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:33.200
What do you say, kid?
Did you find that informative?

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.620
Yes!

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:40.410
Apparently, one of the three
Artifacts we need is here.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.160
A warehouse? No, that's not right.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:47.290
That would have a large entrance
to move cargo in and out of.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.500
We've had eyes on what seems to be an entrance,

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.330
but only two people have
gone in or out in the last week.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.790
That seems suspect.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:54.620
Yeah.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.950
I'll go.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.830
It's too dangerous, mademoiselle.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:03.450
I can't let a beautiful lady go
someplace like that all alone.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.620
Are you saying...?

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.450
Yes, I'm going, too!

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:07.450
Huh?

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.620
I'm sure the two of us
will do quite well together.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.500
Now then, we should go hold
a strategy session, just the two of us--

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.080
Daddy!

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:19.910
How many times do you have to see
a woman and immediately hit on her,

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.290
and end up getting hurt
before you've had enough?!

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:28.290
N-No, it's not like that. I was purely
concerned for Mariah-<i>chan</i>'s safety...

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.910
I'll tell Mommy on you!

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:33.700
Eep! A-A-Anything but that!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.750
Well, I don't care about you, Daddy.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.410
Y-You don't care?

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:42.580
The real question is, what is <i>she </i>doing here?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:47.950
Ah, Jeeves, the tea that
you make is truly remarkable.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:51.540
Your compliment honors me.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.330
Something's fishy here.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:57.830
The two of you aren't planning
something nasty again, are you?

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.500
No, we aren't.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:05.250
I'm having Tomiko keep this
mansion safe while I'm not here.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:09.370
Multiple hostile organizations
have formed a partnership against us.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.250
They are waiting for Mamoru-<i>san</i>
to be away from the Hoshisato home,

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:15.080
when they will definitely launch a strike.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:21.700
I will keep this house safe,
no matter how they come at it.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.250
How do you plan on that?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.790
This really is delicious tea.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.950
Listen to me when I'm talking to you!

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:33.120
Tomiko is on our side now.
You'll have to put up with her.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.790
That's true. I was formally invited
into the Hoshisato home.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:44.700
For my beloved darling, Jeeves' sake, as well.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:50.660
I am <i>terribly </i>grateful for your assurances.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:41.580
Oh, Makoto, what's wrong?
Why are you up so early?

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:46.410
I just woke up early for some reason.
I thought I'd take a stroll.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.040
Hatena, you look like you've
got something on your mind.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.330
Mm-hmm, I was thinking of a finishing attack.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.540
Hmm? A finishing attack?

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:03.700
Mm-hmm. It came up last night,
when I got out of the bath.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.700
Mistress Kana, if you are
going to be a master thief,

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.450
you will need a finishing move, won't you?

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:14.660
Oh, Ema-<i>san</i>, you sound like I'm in a manga.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:18.040
Oh, Maeve-<i>sama </i>has a finishing move, you know.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.330
She does?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:23.500
A secret move that she only uses
in the very tightest of spots,

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.080
that can mean the difference
between life and death.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.790
A finishing move... might be nice...

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:36.370
I mean, it's cool.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.620
So it came out of that.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.450
A finishing move, huh?

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.250
What do you think, Makoto?

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.450
Good question.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:48.200
Having a finishing move would
be heroic and a little bit exciting.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.120
I know, right?

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:56.950
You bet! I need a finishing move!
Achoo! Oh, sorry about that.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:06.290
Let's think up a finishing
move once we get back.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.000
If you stay outside too long
dressed like that, you'll catch a cold.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.160
Oh... Mm-hmm...

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.330
It's just about time.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:25.700
All right, let's proceed as planned.
Are you really going alone?

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:30.290
Yes. Having larger numbers there
with me would just slow me down.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.830
Jeeves, you handle things on this end.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.870
Very good, madam.

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:41.580
Rest easy. The power of love between
Jeeves and me will protect the mansion.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:44.580
I hope so. Well, off I go.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:48.700
Mariah-<i>sama</i>, please do come back safely.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:53.500
Jeeves, you're as much of
a worrier as ever. I'll be fine.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:03.750
I'm not like I was when I was a child.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:12.250
Kokomi-<i>chan</i>, I can't have you
getting involved in a dangerous mission.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:15.040
So be a good girl and go home.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.830
Yeah, I know, already.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.450
Daddy, you be careful, too.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.450
No worries! I'm accustomed
to this sort of thing. Besides,

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.160
I also have <i>this</i>.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.250
Don't overuse it.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:45.950
That Artifact makes your hair fall out
as a toll every time you use it.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:56.370
"Please do come back safely," huh?
Imagine, hearing those words again.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:59.250
I'm no longer a child,
desperately chasing after my sister

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:04.540
so as not to be left behind. I am now...

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:22.370
Tominozawa-<i>sama</i>,
it would appear we have visitors.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:26.750
We do? Well, since I am here to watch the place,

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:29.580
I'll have to give them a warm welcome.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.700
If you would please see
to the eastern rear gate?

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.790
Leave it to me.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.330
Wh-What's that?!

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:43.700
A hostile?!

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:53.870
My, my, hardly worth the trouble of greeting.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.830
Perhaps the fun is just getting started.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:06.370
You naughty boys have no manners.

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:09.750
I'll have to give you all a good hard spanking.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:20.790
Tomi-Tomi's elegant magic...

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:25.500
...can't be stopped by mere gunfire.
You should remember that.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.200
Send in the scepters.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:48.330
This is a surprise. I would not have
expected you to have Brass Scepters.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.910
You certainly have prepared
some decent Artifacts

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:55.410
with which to break down
the door to the house's vault.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:02.410
However, I will not have you taking
this mansion or myself so lightly.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:26.750
I will give you a somewhat--no, make
that a considerably good thrashing.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.790
You can be grateful that my
current master genuinely abhors

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:34.660
allowing an Artifact to
take the life of another.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:44.540
It looks like some kind of research facility.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.580
I'm grateful for the
recognition-inhibiting effect,

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.910
but it kind of takes the fun out of this.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.040
Could that really be the Golden Wings?

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.620
No.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:28.160
It looks similar, but that's a fake.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:34.500
Is it possible they were trying to create
their own Artifacts? Mindboggling.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:38.250
This is unacceptable. Absolutely unacceptable.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:42.410
I was planning on stealing my
objective and sneaking out of here,

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.450
but change of plans!

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:51.200
Okay, Green Servants,
tear this place up as hard as you can!

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:06.410
What? The butler turned young again?!

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.580
What do you mean?! Hey!

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.120
Is something the matter?

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:13.450
It's a call from the men
I sent to the Hoshisato place.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.660
I don't understand what's happening.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.750
That must have you upset.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:27.330
Kikyouin Masayoshi. What brings you here?

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:31.500
Hey, everyone. I thought you might be flustered.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:36.120
I thought I might offer an
explanation and rushed on over.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:40.000
I noticed that you all were
targeting the Hoshisato mansion,

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.290
so I saw about opposing you.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:48.410
Also, I just got a call from Mariah-<i>san</i>.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:51.120
Your research lab--was it?--

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:55.000
apparently had something awful happen to it.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.370
Kikyouin,

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:59.950
you came here just to tell us this?

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.620
Oh, no, no, I'm much too busy for that.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.160
I need you to tell me the location
of the Ring of the Thunder God,

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.120
the Artifact that you are in possession of.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:14.120
It's well known as an Artifact
that does not live up to its name.

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:17.790
A small price to pay for your lives, isn't it?

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:22.450
Do you think we'd be in this
business if we responded to threats?

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:27.660
Oh, no, you don't have to tell me.
I'll just have a little peek.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:34.120
Oh-ho, you didn't leave it at your
mansion, but at your lover's place.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:38.540
The location... isn't that far away, is it?

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:45.620
This is an Artifact that can read
people's minds. It's quite useful.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:50.750
You don't think you're just going
to walk out of here alive, do you?!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:56.250
Old man, for someone who's
been in the business this long,

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.830
you don't have a clue.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:19:58.950
What?!

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.750
If I've made it in here this far,

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:05.250
then you must not know what
happened to your bodyguards.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:10.950
Well now, I think it's time
to get down to business.

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:17.290
Don't forget, I have this, so you can't
lie to me or toss around empty threats!

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:28.040
I rushed back because I thought
you might need some help.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.120
I guess you didn't, huh?

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:34.540
I asked our uninvited guests to please adjourn.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:37.000
Right, "adjourn."

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:40.410
So, how did you fare in your task?

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.000
Very well.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:48.620
Ho, this sure takes me back.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:52.250
It has been a long time since
I have seen the Glyph of the Wind God.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:57.410
Oh dear, I cannot believe I forgot
to greet you upon your return.

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:58.870
Huh?

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:04.120
Welcome home. It is so good
to see you have returned safely.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.620
So then, everything went well on your end?

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.450
After Kikyouin made a cordial request,

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:15.580
they were all too happy to return the Artifact.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.450
You don't say. I'll bet it was "cordial."

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.750
We're just about through
here, too, with no harm done.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:27.450
Although Kikyouin was bellyaching
about losing his hair again.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:32.450
Oh, no, I should be extending
my condolences to Kikyouin.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:36.160
Anyhow, we'll finish up here
and head back as soon as possible.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.790
Mariah and the others have
gotten the Glyph of the Wind God

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.370
and the Ring of the Thunder God.

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:48.200
Huh? Already?!

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.410
Since Mariah and the others
have finished up so quickly,

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:54.330
we'll have to work hard, as well, won't we?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.950
Of course!

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.000
Just you wait, Mama!

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:38.910
"What's a hobby you would like to try?"

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:50.000
"Mamoru"

00:23:52.040 --> 00:24:01.950
"See you next time"
